WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.900
Who leads?

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.838
The book's framing is simple.

3
00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:07.175
Microsoft provides the instruments;
the program provides the orchestra.

4
00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:10.552
Cloud identity, device
management, Conditional Access,

5
00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:15.325
privileged identity management and the
assessment tools are each excellent.

6
00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:17.375
But look at what each one doesn't decide.

7
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:21.800
Cloud identity doesn't decide what your
organizational structure should become.

8
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.150
Hybrid management doesn't
decide which servers retire.

9
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.575
The assessment tools don't decide
what to do with the findings.

10
00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:32.287
Every entry in that column is
a decision someone has to own.

11
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:37.214
And no vendor deadline forces it, so
without leadership organizations migrate in

12
00:00:37.214 --> 00:00:41.850
pieces and finish with a surface that
can't answer last year's audit questions.

13
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.908
And the program isn't a product:
it needs no license of its own,

14
00:00:45.908 --> 00:00:49.718
but the services it orchestrates
do, from Entra ID P1 for

15
00:00:49.718 --> 00:00:54.438
Conditional Access to Entra ID
Governance for lifecycle workflows.

16
00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:58.826
Federal policy already says this
belongs to more than the IT shop.

17
00:00:58.826 --> 00:01:04.665
M-22-09 says the whole C-suite must be
aligned and committed, and it required

18
00:01:04.665 --> 00:01:09.612
each agency to designate a zero trust
implementation lead within 30 days.

19
00:01:09.612 --> 00:01:15.841
M-19-17 requires an agency-wide identity
governance structure that includes HR,

20
00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:18.600
general counsel, privacy and acquisition.

21
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.835
So the first Who decision, for the
sponsor and the CIO before Phase 0:

22
00:01:22.835 --> 00:01:25.300
confirm who already holds those roles,

23
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.210
and decide whether one of them
becomes the program's steward.
